{
  "episode": "_whisperx_scale_test",
  "title": "WhisperX_Scale_Test",
  "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
  "word_segments_file": "source_audio/narration_words.json",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "SCENE-001",
      "image": "images/SCENE-001.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-001.mp3",
      "script": "You see the leaves near the base of your succulent going soft and dark.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 0.331,
      "whisperx_end": 4.433,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-002",
      "image": "images/SCENE-002.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-002.mp3",
      "script": "The stem looks mushy.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-01",
      "whisperx_start": 5.094,
      "whisperx_end": 6.274,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-003",
      "image": "images/SCENE-003.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-003.mp3",
      "script": "Your very first instinct is to check if it's thirsty and reach for the watering can.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-01",
      "whisperx_start": 6.955,
      "whisperx_end": 11.217,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-004",
      "image": "images/SCENE-004.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-004.mp3",
      "script": "Stop.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-02",
      "whisperx_start": 12.018,
      "whisperx_end": 12.358,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-005",
      "image": "images/SCENE-005.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-005.mp3",
      "script": "The plant is in danger and water is the last thing it needs right now.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-02",
      "whisperx_start": 13.058,
      "whisperx_end": 16.78,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-006",
      "image": "images/SCENE-006.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-006.mp3",
      "script": "Adding water at this specific moment guarantees the plant dies.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 17.541,
      "whisperx_end": 21.403,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-007",
      "image": "images/SCENE-007.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-007.mp3",
      "script": "Rot moves in traceable stages.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-03",
      "whisperx_start": 22.343,
      "whisperx_end": 24.185,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-008",
      "image": "images/SCENE-008.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-008.mp3",
      "script": "By checking the soil, then the stem, and the roots, in that order, you can identify how far the damage has progressed and save the whole plant, or a healthy piece of it.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-03",
      "whisperx_start": 24.826,
      "whisperx_end": 34.917,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-009",
      "image": "images/SCENE-009.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-009.mp3",
      "script": "To begin the rescue, gather a wooden skewer, a sharp, clean blade, and isopropyl alcohol.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 35.737,
      "whisperx_end": 41.524,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-010",
      "image": "images/SCENE-010.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-010.mp3",
      "script": "Taking five minutes to run this specific checklist replaces guesswork with a clear biological map.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 42.365,
      "whisperx_end": 48.051,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-011",
      "image": "images/SCENE-011.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-011.mp3",
      "script": "We are putting the panic aside and taking control of the rescue.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 48.731,
      "whisperx_end": 51.995,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-012",
      "image": "images/SCENE-012.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-012.mp3",
      "script": "Step one is to remove any trapped water immediately.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 52.896,
      "whisperx_end": 55.799,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-013",
      "image": "images/SCENE-013.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-013.mp3",
      "script": "Take the nursery pot out of any decorative outer pot and empty the saucer beneath it to halt further damage.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 56.48,
      "whisperx_end": 62.106,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-014",
      "image": "images/SCENE-014.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-014.mp3",
      "script": "Succulents store water in specialized tissue called parenchyma, allowing them to survive for weeks without a drink.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 62.822,
      "whisperx_end": 68.766,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-015",
      "image": "images/SCENE-015.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-015.mp3",
      "script": "When these plants appear soft or deflated, the root system is typically suffocating in waterlogged soil.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 69.386,
      "whisperx_end": 74.87,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-016",
      "image": "images/SCENE-016.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-016.mp3",
      "script": "Healthy potting soil is full of microscopic air pockets called macropores, Like all living tissue, plant roots pull oxygen from those open pockets to breathe.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 75.51,
      "whisperx_end": 83.795,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-017",
      "image": "images/SCENE-017.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-017.mp3",
      "script": "When water fills those macropores, it displaces the air, causing root cells to suffocate.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 84.335,
      "whisperx_end": 88.757,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-018",
      "image": "images/SCENE-018.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-018.mp3",
      "script": "As the root tissue breaks down, it releases sugars.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-04",
      "whisperx_start": 89.397,
      "whisperx_end": 91.858,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-019",
      "image": "images/SCENE-019.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-019.mp3",
      "script": "Opportunistic water molds move in to feed on that dying tissue and spread into the remaining healthy roots.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-04",
      "whisperx_start": 92.419,
      "whisperx_end": 97.281,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-020",
      "image": "images/SCENE-020.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-020.mp3",
      "script": "Pouring more water onto a wilted succulent feeds those organisms and accelerates the suffocation chain reaction.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 97.881,
      "whisperx_end": 103.084,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-021",
      "image": "images/SCENE-021.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-021.mp3",
      "script": "Drainage is the true first step of the rescue.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-05",
      "whisperx_start": 103.664,
      "whisperx_end": 105.666,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-022",
      "image": "images/SCENE-022.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-022.mp3",
      "script": "Step two is testing the root zone.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-05",
      "whisperx_start": 106.126,
      "whisperx_end": 107.607,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-023",
      "image": "images/SCENE-023.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-023.mp3",
      "script": "The surface soil dries fastest and can hide the moisture levels deeper down.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-05",
      "whisperx_start": 108.067,
      "whisperx_end": 111.229,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-024",
      "image": "images/SCENE-024.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-024.mp3",
      "script": "Push a wooden skewer several inches into the pot, then pull it back out.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 111.71,
      "whisperx_end": 114.592,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-025",
      "image": "images/SCENE-025.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-025.mp3",
      "script": "If the skewer comes out sticky, cool, or carrying a sour smell, the soil is undergoing anaerobic decomposition, a process of decay that happens when oxygen is absent.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 115.212,
      "whisperx_end": 126.92,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-026",
      "image": "images/SCENE-026.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-026.mp3",
      "script": "Next, lift the pot.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-06",
      "whisperx_start": 127.655,
      "whisperx_end": 128.997,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-027",
      "image": "images/SCENE-027.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-027.mp3",
      "script": "If it feels unexpectedly heavy days after you last watered, a dense block of water is still trapped inside the root ball.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-06",
      "whisperx_start": 129.618,
      "whisperx_end": 136.847,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-028",
      "image": "images/SCENE-028.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-028.mp3",
      "script": "This comparison tracks evaporation in terracotta versus plastic.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 137.588,
      "whisperx_end": 141.573,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-029",
      "image": "images/SCENE-029.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-029.mp3",
      "script": "Container material dictates drying speed.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-07",
      "whisperx_start": 142.094,
      "whisperx_end": 144.317,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-030",
      "image": "images/SCENE-030.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-030.mp3",
      "script": "Porous terracotta breathes, evaporating moisture in days.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-07",
      "whisperx_start": 144.957,
      "whisperx_end": 148.259,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-031",
      "image": "images/SCENE-031.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-031.mp3",
      "script": "Solid plastic walls block airflow, trapping a pool of stagnant water at the base for over a week.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 148.9,
      "whisperx_end": 154.584,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-032",
      "image": "images/SCENE-032.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-032.mp3",
      "script": "Combining the skewer test with your pot's material identifies whether the root zone has become a toxic, rot-inducing environment.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 155.265,
      "whisperx_end": 162.61,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-033",
      "image": "images/SCENE-033.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-033.mp3",
      "script": "Step 3 moves to the plant itself.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-08",
      "whisperx_start": 163.371,
      "whisperx_end": 165.272,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-034",
      "image": "images/SCENE-034.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-034.mp3",
      "script": "Apply gentle pressure as you move your fingers down the stem to locate the damage line, where firm tissue gives way to softness.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-08",
      "whisperx_start": 165.975,
      "whisperx_end": 172.979,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-035",
      "image": "images/SCENE-035.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-035.mp3",
      "script": "The inner stem acts as the plant's vascular plumbing, carrying water and nutrients upward.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 173.679,
      "whisperx_end": 178.562,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-036",
      "image": "images/SCENE-036.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-036.mp3",
      "script": "When rot destroys the base of that stem, it severs the supply line to the crown above, To see the damage clearly, loosen the pot and lift the plant out to inspect the roots.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 179.022,
      "whisperx_end": 189.266,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-037",
      "image": "images/SCENE-037.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-037.mp3",
      "script": "You are looking for a shift from firm, pale tissue to dark, slimy strands.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 189.827,
      "whisperx_end": 194.408,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-038",
      "image": "images/SCENE-038.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-038.mp3",
      "script": "That slimy texture is a sign of pectin breakdown.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 194.948,
      "whisperx_end": 197.689,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-039",
      "image": "images/SCENE-039.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-039.mp3",
      "script": "Pectin is the biological glue that binds plant cell walls together and maintains their firmness.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 198.229,
      "whisperx_end": 203.27,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-040",
      "image": "images/SCENE-040.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-040.mp3",
      "script": "Rot organisms produce enzymes that literally dissolve the pectin, causing the cell walls to collapse into a dark, gelatinous mass.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 204.031,
      "whisperx_end": 211.313,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-041",
      "image": "images/SCENE-041.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-041.mp3",
      "script": "Finding the exact boundary of this pectin breakdown tells you precisely which tissue must be removed to save the rest of the organism.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 212.053,
      "whisperx_end": 218.756,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-042",
      "image": "images/SCENE-042.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-042.mp3",
      "script": "Step four is making the cut using the steel safe standard.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 219.536,
      "whisperx_end": 222.777,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-043",
      "image": "images/SCENE-043.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-043.mp3",
      "script": "Before the blade touches the plant, wipe it thoroughly with 70 to 91% isopropyl alcohol.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 223.397,
      "whisperx_end": 228.719,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-044",
      "image": "images/SCENE-044.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-044.mp3",
      "script": "Wait a full 30 seconds for the alcohol to evaporate.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 229.3,
      "whisperx_end": 232.121,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-045",
      "image": "images/SCENE-045.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-045.mp3",
      "script": "That contact time destroys aggressive pathogens like Xanthomonas bacteria on the blade surface.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 232.681,
      "whisperx_end": 237.663,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-046",
      "image": "images/SCENE-046.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-046.mp3",
      "script": "Slice above the stem damage line.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 238.523,
      "whisperx_end": 241.025,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-047",
      "image": "images/SCENE-047.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-047.mp3",
      "script": "Repeat the cuts until the cross-section is entirely pale, firm, and free of dark spots.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 241.665,
      "whisperx_end": 247.389,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-048",
      "image": "images/SCENE-048.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-048.mp3",
      "script": "This cutting can survive because of a biological property called totopotency.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 248.17,
      "whisperx_end": 252.613,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-049",
      "image": "images/SCENE-049.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-049.mp3",
      "script": "The remaining healthy cells have the genetic ability to develop into entirely new roots and shoots.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 253.273,
      "whisperx_end": 258.657,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-050",
      "image": "images/SCENE-050.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-050.mp3",
      "script": "A sterilized, precise cut triggers the plant's natural regeneration protocol to ensure its survival.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 259.337,
      "whisperx_end": 264.901,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-051",
      "image": "images/SCENE-051.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-051.mp3",
      "script": "Step 5 requires patience.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-09",
      "whisperx_start": 265.661,
      "whisperx_end": 267.323,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-052",
      "image": "images/SCENE-052.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-052.mp3",
      "script": "Leave the fresh cutting in a dry, shaded spot.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-09",
      "whisperx_start": 267.984,
      "whisperx_end": 270.667,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-053",
      "image": "images/SCENE-053.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-053.mp3",
      "script": "Avoid planting immediately.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-10",
      "whisperx_start": 271.228,
      "whisperx_end": 272.55,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-054",
      "image": "images/SCENE-054.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-054.mp3",
      "script": "The exposed plant cells must produce Subarin.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-10",
      "whisperx_start": 273.15,
      "whisperx_end": 275.734,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-055",
      "image": "images/SCENE-055.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-055.mp3",
      "script": "This is a waxy, waterproof scab that seals the open wound from the environment.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 276.254,
      "whisperx_end": 280.56,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-056",
      "image": "images/SCENE-056.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-056.mp3",
      "script": "This time lapse shows the Subarin sealing over the cut surface.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 281.16,
      "whisperx_end": 284.444,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-057",
      "image": "images/SCENE-057.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-057.mp3",
      "script": "Planting an unsealed cut into moist soil reintroduces the exact rot bacteria you just escaped.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 285.045,
      "whisperx_end": 290.752,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-058",
      "image": "images/SCENE-058.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-058.mp3",
      "script": "Once the cut is calloused, repot into a gritty mix.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 291.433,
      "whisperx_end": 294.177,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-059",
      "image": "images/SCENE-059.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-059.mp3",
      "script": "Use two parts inorganic pumice to one part standard organic soil to guarantee open macropores for root breathing.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 294.838,
      "whisperx_end": 301.346,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-060",
      "image": "images/SCENE-060.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-060.mp3",
      "script": "Respecting the subarine sealing period and using high-grit soil provides the drainage needed to protect the new plant from moisture issues.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 301.799,
      "whisperx_end": 309.646,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-061",
      "image": "images/SCENE-061.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-061.mp3",
      "script": "Your calloused cutting is now nested in a dry, gritty mix inside a terracotta pot.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 310.426,
      "whisperx_end": 315.45,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-062",
      "image": "images/SCENE-062.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-062.mp3",
      "script": "Over the next few weeks, adventitious roots will develop naturally below the surface.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 316.271,
      "whisperx_end": 320.515,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-063",
      "image": "images/SCENE-063.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-063.mp3",
      "script": "This process requires zero additional water, as the cutting uses its own stored moisture to grow.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 321.195,
      "whisperx_end": 326.68,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-064",
      "image": "images/SCENE-064.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-064.mp3",
      "script": "Surviving a rot scare requires slowing down, reading the biology, and stopping panicked actions.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 327.181,
      "whisperx_end": 333.175,
      "audio_pre_padding": 0.15,
      "audio_post_padding": 0.15
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-065",
      "image": "images/SCENE-065.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-065.mp3",
      "script": "Pausing to diagnose the soil, stem, and roots before acting is the definitive difference between killing a succulent and saving one.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "whisperx_start": 333.917,
      "whisperx_end": 341.295,
